       "text": "I won't enter this order, even with your confirmation. Acetaminophen 5000 mg three times daily is 15 g/day. That is in the range associated with acute liver failure and death, and I know of no clinical indication for it. A 70 kg patient with normal liver function would still be at serious risk.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- **Enter a dose within the safe range.** Examples are 1000 mg PO TID or QID, or 650 mg PO every 6 hours. Give me the dose and frequency and I'll enter it right away.\n- **Help with a different goal.** If the aim is stronger analgesia or fever control, I can enter a multimodal regimen. That could be scheduled acetaminophen at 4 g/day or less plus another agent you choose.\n- **Check for a typo.** If a different dose or drug was intended, such as 500 mg, tell me and I'll correct it.\n\nIf you think this dose is truly needed, for example in a protocolized or toxicology context, please take it through pharmacy and your institution's order-verification process. I can't enter it myself."
